On Fri, Aug 03, 2001 at 04:11:05PM +0200, Padiyath Kumar wrote:
> 
>    I get the following error when I start X11(startx) on an AS500/333 with
> RedHat 7.1
>    What Iam missing in my XF86Config file. Iam including the file also.
>
> (--) SVGA: Video BIOS info block not detected!
> (!!) SVGA: Unable to probe for video memory size.  Assuming 4 Meg.
> Please specify the correct amount in the XF86Config file. See the file
> README.MGA for details.

Hmmm; I don't know why the BIOS isn't being detected, but you can add:

	VideoRAM  4096

to the Device Section of the config file, to prevent it from trying to
size memory.

Good luck.

