Hello !
Once again I try to get our Ruffian stable. We now moved him into a colder
room but he remains quite instable, many things simply cause memory faults,
i.e. some grep, cp, ...

I noticed that the part just below the memory sticks gets very hot, even
if the machine was turned off for several hours. 

It is a Ruffian (UX) with 2*256 MB Ram. I tried to boot with a single 
memory stick but it did not boot. 

Does anyone have a suggestion to single out the faulty part ? Would it
be sensbile to add extra coolers (i.e. for the memory) or is there some
"tricky" programm to single out the "true" memory problem (if it is
such).

Thanks

       Helge
