Hello !
On Wed, Aug 08, 2001 at 10:05:21AM +0200, Peter Bech wrote:
> Ineiti wrote:
> I should answer you directly to avoid beinmg diculed, but it's because th=
e=20
> clock is not running correctly on the DS10. Reboot adjusts it correctly.

No need to reboot here. Simply add:
18 * * * *  /usr/sbin/ntpdate -s YourFavoriteTimeServer
in your crontab (i.e. as root crontab -e).

Either you set up a local time server (maybe you can get the german
radio signal and pick up a radio controlled clock and attach it to one
of your machines) or check out public time servers. Simply search for
it on google and you'll find sites like:

http://www.eecis.udel.edu/~mills/ntp/servers.html

with more information.

kreutzm@menkar:~[568] % rpm -qf /usr/sbin/ntpdate
xntp3-5.93-14
(on RH 6.2 Intel).

Regards

