Has anybody managed to get XFree4.0.3 or 4.1.0 rpms running stable on
UP2000? The 4.0.3 rpms coming with RH7.1 invariably hang our two UP2000s
within a few minutes. Recompiling & installing 4.1.0-0.9.6 from rawhide
didn't improve anything. I'm pretty sure this is not a kernel
problem: The problem didn't go away when upgrading from the stock rh7.1
kernel (2.4.3-12) to 2.4.7, or to 2.2.19.
On the positive side, a XFree 4.1.0 recompile from the xfree86 source
tarball works nicely, and with all the kernels (but without
HW acceleration so far), and we don't have seen any problem on both a
XP1000 (same RH7.1 CD, same voodoo3 graphics card) and a PC164 (rh7.1,
matrox mill card).
So I guess this is a specific problem with the additional patches within
the rpms on UP2000s. Does anybody have similar experience and/or a
solution?
I'd appreciate any help.

Oliver




