Hello !
On Wed, Aug 08, 2001 at 01:35:16PM +0200, g.j.kuiper@kpn.com wrote:
> Why use ntp at all ? The hardware clock is fine - otherwise rebooting
> wouldn't help either. So just setting the system time from the hardware
> clock should be sufficient. The command for that can be found somewhere in
> the rc files.

You are right. 
hwclock --hctosys
(and possible other options -- check the man page). 
as a regular cron job should suffice in this case. Still if you have a
couple of systems I would recommend xntp in any case -- if just to keep
make happy on nfs :-)) (even if all clocks are accurate setting them
to the exact same value manually is not nice).

Greetings

        Helge
