On Wed, Aug 08, 2001 at 05:19:51PM +0200, g.j.kuiper@kpn.com wrote:
> 
> I have the same thing on my PC164, even with both cards being NCR/SYMBIOS
> (one 810, one 875). I solved it by accepting the new names, i.e. I edited
> fstab and abootconf.

Ah, now *that* problem can be solved via boot command argument, or at
least it used to be possible. Or you could try switching the PCI slots
of the two controllers, so that the desired one is probed first.

By adding "pci=reverse" to the boot flags, the order of the PCI
devices probed is reversed, so controllers in higher slot numbers are
handled before controllers in the lower slot numbers.

--Jay++

