The soundcard is a "good" old ISA SoundBlaster16 (NO PnP).
It is working perfect with linux 2.2.x (19)

But wenn trying to play a sound with kernel 2.4.x (tried with 6 and 7)
no sound comes. Instead a terrible noise comes out of the boxes. The
interrupt and the DMA channels are correct (proved in /proc).

I tried it also with other ISA cards I have access to (e.g. AWE64) with
and without PnP but the result is always the same. I tried both the
kernel PnP support and the isapnp tools (thats what I am using in
2.2.x).

I think I have tried all possible tricks. 

Any suggestions other then bying a PCI soundcard :-)

Max

