After troubleshooting to the best of my abilities I believe the DEC =
Server 3300 will not run Redhat 7.1 due to a problem with the driver for =
the onboard Qlogic SCSI controller.  I have not tried the BSD Qlogic =
driver that Jay suggested.  That sounds difficult :P

Aaron Brueck
  ----- Original Message -----=20
  From: Kurt Ludwig=20
  To: axp-list@redhat.com=20
  Sent: Tuesday, August 14, 2001 9:36 AM
  Subject: RE: DEC Server 3300 and Redhat 7.1


  ok another question.... is the CDRom that you are installing from a =
CDR or a CDRW? I've seen quite a few problems with older CDRoms using =
CDRWs.

  Kurt

    -----Original Message-----
    From: axp-list-admin@redhat.com [mailto:axp-list-admin@redhat.com]On =
Behalf Of Alexey Chupakhin
    Sent: Tuesday, August 14, 2001 9:40 AM
    To: axp-list@redhat.com
    Subject: Re: DEC Server 3300 and Redhat 7.1


    I have exactly same problem with Celeron-366 and RH 6.2 some times =
ago. The reason was.... durty disk and bad CD-ROM.
    I clean both and installed system well.

      ----- Original Message -----=20
      From: Aaron Brueck=20
      To: axp-list@redhat.com=20
      Sent: Thursday, August 09, 2001 4:50 PM
      Subject: DEC Server 3300 and Redhat 7.1


      I am unable to load Redhat 7.1 on a DEC Server 3300.  The install =
crashes at a random point while it is installing packages.  I've tried =
both the graphical and text based install.  I do have some non-standard =
hardware in this machine, but it all works fine with Redhat 7.0.  In =
fact I have reloaded 7.0 and am up and running again.  Does anyone have =
experience with the 3300 server and RH 7.1?  I realize it's an oddball =
machine, originally designed to run NT, but it does have a SRM console.

      Aaron Brueck

