We are currently using the bigphysarea patch from
http://www.uni-paderborn.de/cs/heiss/linux/bigphysarea.html for our 2.2
series kernels on the Alpha.  This patch allows a big physical area of ram
to be mapped between kernel mode and user mode for direct memory access.
>From the page above:

The Linux kernel is optimized for managing many small pieces of memory,
usually one page at a time. The largest continuous block that can be
allocated is 128Kb (default value). Some drivers need much larger blocks,
e.g. drivers for framegrabbers, high speed A/D converters or our SCI driver.

Is this patch required for a 2.4 kernel?  If not, what API replaces it.
